IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-solvency`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): part sga1, module 5.
-- Part 4, Division 3 (shares): s 70, redeemable preference shares.
--
-- Every function answers MAYBE (BOOLEAN, NUMBER ...): JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga1)") has the rule of 2026-10-29 and the two readings "for a lawyer".
-- Seam taken from the keel: s 70(4)(a) asks `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` of the core's `Solvency statement`, with the proposal
-- `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70` (PLAN.md seam B).

§ `Section 70: redeemable preference shares`

-- (1) the power to issue, and the "only" on the terms and manner of redemption.
-- src:6853 | 70.—(1) Subject to this section, a company having a share capital
-- src:6854 | may, if so authorised by its constitution, issue preference shares
-- src:6855 | which are, or at the option of the company are to be, liable to be
-- src:6856 | redeemed and the redemption may be effected only on such terms and
-- src:6857 | in such manner as is provided by the constitution.
@ref s 70(1) (src:6853-6857)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company authorises the company to issue preference shares that are, or at the option of the company are to be, liable to be redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(1) the company may issue preference shares that are liable to be redeemed` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital` AND `the constitution of the company authorises the company to issue preference shares that are, or at the option of the company are to be, liable to be redeemed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company having a share capital may, if so authorised by its constitution, issue preference shares" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1); the subsection does not say the company may not

@ref s 70(1) (src:6853-6857)
GIVEN `the shares are preference shares that are, or at the option of the company are to be, liable to be redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the redemption is effected on the terms and in the manner provided by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(1) the redemption may be effected` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are preference shares that are, or at the option of the company are to be, liable to be redeemed`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "preference shares which are, or at the option of the company are to be, liable to be redeemed" -- other shares are not covered
    ELSE (IF `the redemption is effected on the terms and in the manner provided by the constitution`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the redemption may be effected only on such terms and in such manner as is provided by the constitution" -- an "only" the redemption does not meet

-- (3) the bar on redeeming shares that are not fully paid up. JUST TRUE is barred.
-- src:6863 | (3) The shares must not be redeemed unless they are fully paid up.
@ref s 70(3) (src:6863)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemable preference shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are fully paid up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(3) the company is barred from redeeming the shares` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are redeemable preference shares`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The shares" -- the shares of subsection (1); other shares are not covered
    ELSE (IF `the shares are fully paid up`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be redeemed unless they are fully paid up" -- the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 70 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 70(3) redeem shares that are not fully paid up`
    `s 70(4) redeem shares out of capital without a solvency statement made by all the directors and lodged`
    `s 70(8) give notice to the Registrar specifying the shares redeemed`

@ref s 70(3) (src:6863)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 70 act`
`s 70(3) a company must not redeem shares that are not fully paid up` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 70(3) redeem shares that are not fully paid up`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company redeemed redeemable preference shares that were not fully paid up"

-- (4) the bar on redeeming out of capital without a solvency statement made by all the directors and lodged. JUST TRUE is barred.
-- The statement is the core's record; the keel decides whether it is a solvency statement (s 7A(1)); this function adds that it concerns this redemption,
-- that all the directors made it, and that a copy was lodged.
-- src:6865 | (4) The shares must not be redeemed out of the capital of the
-- src:6866 | company unless —
-- src:6871 | (a) all the directors have made a solvency statement in relation
-- src:6872 | to such redemption; and
-- src:6874 | (b) the company has lodged a copy of the statement with the
-- src:6875 | Registrar.
@ref s 70(4) (src:6865-6875)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemed out of the capital of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      statement IS A `Solvency statement`
      `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directors of the company have made the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged a copy of the statement with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(4) the company is barred from redeeming the shares out of capital` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are redeemed out of the capital of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not be redeemed out of the capital of the company" -- a redemption out of other money is not covered
    ELSE (IF     (statement's `the proposal it concerns` EQUALS `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`)
             AND (`s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` statement `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             AND `all the directors of the company have made the statement`
             AND `the company has lodged a copy of the statement with the Registrar`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless -- (a) all the directors have made a solvency statement in relation to such redemption; and (b) the company has lodged a copy of the statement with the Registrar" -- the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 70(4) (src:6865-6875)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 70 act`
`s 70(4) a company must not redeem shares out of capital without a solvency statement made by all the directors and lodged` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 70(4) redeem shares out of capital without a solvency statement made by all the directors and lodged`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company redeemed redeemable preference shares out of capital without a solvency statement made by all the directors and a copy lodged with the Registrar"

-- (5) the avoidance of doubt: redemption out of the proceeds of a fresh issue is not redemption out of capital.
-- src:6877 | (5) To avoid doubt, shares redeemed out of proceeds of a fresh issue
-- src:6878 | of shares issued for the purpose of redemption are not to be treated as
-- src:6879 | having been redeemed out of the capital of the company.
@ref s 70(5) (src:6877-6879)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemed out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares issued for the purpose of redemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(5) the shares are treated as redeemed out of the capital of the company` MEANS
    IF `the shares are redeemed out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares issued for the purpose of redemption`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shares redeemed out of proceeds of a fresh issue of shares issued for the purpose of redemption are not to be treated as having been redeemed out of the capital of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares redeemed out of proceeds of a fresh issue of shares issued for the purpose of redemption" -- another source is not covered

-- (6) a private company's redemption by notice.
-- src:6883 | (6) A private company may redeem any redeemable preference
-- src:6884 | shares by lodging a prescribed notice of redemption with the
-- src:6885 | Registrar.
@ref s 70(6) (src:6883-6885)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are redeemable preference shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prescribed notice of redemption has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(6) the private company may redeem the shares by lodging the notice` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `the shares are redeemable preference shares` AND `a prescribed notice of redemption has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may redeem any redeemable preference shares by lodging a prescribed notice of redemption with the Registrar" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (7) the redemption by a private company does not take effect until the register is updated.
-- src:6889 | (7) A redemption of any redeemable preference shares by a private
-- src:6890 | company on or after 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the
-- src:6891 | electronic register of members of the company is updated by the
-- src:6892 | Registrar under section 196A(5).
@ref s 70(7) (src:6889-6892)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the redemption` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(7) the redemption has not yet taken effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR `the day of the redemption` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A redemption of any redeemable preference shares by a private company on or after 3 January 2016" -- a public company or a redemption before 3 January 2016 is not covered (periods ruling (c); fork F-X1)
    ELSE (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)" -- the register has been updated, so the bar is over
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (8) a public company's notice of redemption within 14 days. Asked as "in default": JUST TRUE where the notice is late, absent after the 14 days, or does not specify the shares redeemed.
-- src:6896 | (8) If a public company redeems any redeemable preference shares,
-- src:6897 | it must within 14 days after doing so give notice thereof to the
-- src:6898 | Registrar specifying the shares redeemed.
@ref s 70(8) (src:6896-6898)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has redeemed redeemable preference shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the redemption` IS A DATE
      `notice of the redemption has been given to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the notice specifies the shares redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(8) the public company is in default of the duty to give notice to the Registrar of the redemption` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is a public company` AND `the company has redeemed redeemable preference shares`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a public company redeems any redeemable preference shares, it must within 14 days after doing so give notice" -- a failed "if" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise
    ELSE (IF `notice of the redemption has been given to the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the redemption` `the day the notice was given` 14 Days AND `the notice specifies the shares redeemed`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within 14 days after doing so give notice thereof to the Registrar specifying the shares redeemed" -- the notice came within the 14 days (a period the text fixes: periods ruling (a)) and specifies the shares
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the redemption` 14 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after doing so" -- the 14 days have not yet run out (periods ruling (a))

@ref s 70(8) (src:6896-6898)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 70 act`
`s 70(8) a public company must give notice to the Registrar of the redemption within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 70(8) give notice to the Registrar specifying the shares redeemed`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not give notice to the Registrar specifying the shares redeemed within 14 days after the redemption"
